Package: atuin-ai
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, atuin
Description: AI shell agent for Atuin, talking to a self-hosted server
 Atuin AI is the shell agent Atuin shipped up to 18.24, now a standalone
 binary. Press ? at an empty prompt to chat: it suggests commands and answers
 questions, and with your permission it can search your Atuin history, read
 and edit files, and run commands.
 .
 It needs an Atuin AI server, which you host yourself (upstream publishes a
 Docker image), backed by any OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Set endpoint in
 ~/.atuin/ai.toml, then add eval "$(atuin-ai init bash)" (or zsh, fish) after
 Atuin's own init. This package is a weekly snapshot of upstream's main
 branch, which has no releases.
